==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|en}} {{term|repulsif|lang=frm}}, from {{etyl|ML.|en}} {{term|repulsivus|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|/rĭ-pŭl'sĭv/|/rē-pŭl'sĭv/}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# tending to rouse [[aversion]] or to [[repulse]]
# {{context|physics|lang=en}} having the [[capacity]] to [[repel]]

====Usage notes====
* Nouns to which "repulsive" is often applied: force, interaction, potential.

====Synonyms====
* [[repellent]]
* similar:  [[disgusting]], [[vile]]

====Antonyms====
* (''tending to rouse aversion'') [[attractive]]
* (''physics, having the capacity to repel'') [[attractive]]

